inet: build accept4 only when there is a system call for it

With kernel headers that have neither __NR_accept4 nor __NR_socketcall (ARM
EABI before Linux 2.6.36), socketcalls.c still built accept4, with an empty
body: it made no system call and returned 0. Every other call without a
system call is left out of libc (or, with UCLIBC_HAS_STUBS, is a stub in
stubs.c failing with ENOSYS). GLib found accept4 and used it:
g_socket_accept() took the 0 as the new connection (descriptor 0, stdin), and
the controller, serving applications through a GSocketService, looped on it.
Left out, programs configure without it (GLib then calls accept).

--- a/libc/inet/socketcalls.c
+++ b/libc/inet/socketcalls.c
@@ -80,7 +80,9 @@
 lt_libc_hidden(accept)
 #endif

-#ifdef L_accept4
+/* Only with a system call for it, like the calls stubs.c covers: an empty
+   one would return 0. */
+#if defined(L_accept4) && (defined(__NR_accept4) || defined(__NR_socketcall))
 static int __NC(accept4)(int fd, struct sockaddr *addr, socklen_t *addrlen, int flags)
 {
 # ifdef __NR_accept4
